WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:06.270
Michael Santana streams League of
Legends to almost 20,000 viewers every

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.280
day.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:19.600
He's on a self-motivated quest to
become the best AD carry in North America

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.700
He makes over 1.5

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:39.030
million dollars every year from the
comfort of his own living room, alongside

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.420
his trusty sidekicks small cat and
mellow.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:56.540
He's a QTPie and this is his story.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.600
Michael "Imaqtpie" Santana's

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.820
professional League of Legends career
started in 2011, right around the time

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:25.060
that the LCS was being formed. He was
recruited by William "Scarra" Li to join his

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:30.600
team Rock Solid as their starting AD
carry. Soon after they formed, the team

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:35.690
finished fourth at the National ESL
Premier League in 2011 and were picked

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:41.869
up by Dignitas. Dig's initial lineup
consisted of Voyboy in the top lane, Jatt

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:46.940
in the jungle, Scarra in the mid lane, and
Imaqtpie and Locust in the bot

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:51.920
lane. Their first event under the
Dignitas banner was a massive success as

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:58.300
they defeated Curse Gaming, CLG and Epik
Gamer to win IGN Premier League Season 3.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:03.700
(Casting)

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:07.920
(Casting)

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:11.450
(Casting)

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:16.060
(Casting)

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:23.200
(Casting)

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:27.360
The win helped establish
Dig as a legitimate contender in North

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:32.690
American League of Legends. This was a
time when NA's competitive League of

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:37.560
Legends scene was a far cry from the
structured franchised League it is today.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:41.560
To compete at the highest level teams
had to drop the rest of their

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:46.040
responsibilities and devote their lives
to the game in order to become relevant

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.640
and often unsuccessful trips to
tournaments were a net loss financially.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:57.860
"So initially, it was really a gamble. Because a lot of us were doing it out of passion and there almost no

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:06.440
revenue streams. So there was a point in time, where it cost more to travel to Cologne, for ESL's events

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:13.680
then it did to win third place. So you had to place second or first, to actually get your money back

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.880
for travelling like all the way from North America to Cologne."

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.200
So when Dig bowed out of IEM New

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.480
York's 2012 group stage, it was a big
deal.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:29.140
(Casting)

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:33.190
(Casting)

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:38.880
(Casting)

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:43.380
Dignitas saw season
2 as an opportunity to become a force in

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:49.330
the scene. They placed third at IEM Kiev
which helped them qualify for the IEM

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:53.830
6 World Championship where they lost
to Moscow5 in the finals.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:58.000
QTs performance in Kiev was
impressive, posting a 4.17

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.209
KDA while averaging 4.88

00:04:01.209 --> 00:04:04.200
kills per game throughout the tournament

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:12.300
(Casting)

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:17.320
(Casting)

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:21.820
(Casting)

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.390
(Casting)

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:28.360
(Casting)

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:32.500
(Casting)

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.820
Aside from imaqtpie's stable
presence in the bot lane, Team Dignitas'

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:43.420
roster was a bit of a revolving door.
Jatt stepped down late in 2011 and was

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:49.390
replaced with Iwilldominate early in
2012. Crumbzz was picked up to fill the

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:54.220
hole left in the top lane by Voyboy's
departure. Throughout his career

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:58.990
Imaqtpie was one of the only
members of Dignitas that wasn't in and

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:03.280
out of the lineup and acted as a
stabilizing presence for a lineup that

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:08.590
was constantly in flux. Team Dignitas
were still finding themselves as a team

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:14.860
at the end of Season 2 and into 2013.
Iwilldominate left and Crumbzz went

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:19.800
back to the jungle while KiWiKiD was
signed on to be the team's new top laner.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.420
That core along with qtpie would
eventually become the team's backbone

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:28.300
ahead of the North American LCS' inaugural season.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:34.300
"Season 3 for me is the first step that Riot takes to make this game be like a real sport.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.920
And so there will be a lot of eyes on this first season."

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:39.100
The creation of the North American

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.810
League of Legends Championship Series
saw eight teams from the region compete

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:47.740
in a structured league that was loosely
modeled off of traditional sports

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.430
leagues. "Ladies and gentlemen today is
the day, the official start of the League

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:55.000
of Legends Championship Series. This is a
groundbreaking moment in League history

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:59.260
as eight North American teams take their
first steps on the way to the Summoner's

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:03.760
Cup." For qtpie the NA LCS was a
chance to prove himself

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:09.640
among the region's best players every
week. In the beginning the LCS didn't

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:13.990
have an identity and each of the eight
participating teams were quite different

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:17.680
from one another.
You had the likes of Counter Logic

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:22.600
Gaming and Team SoloMid, established
organizations that had amassed massive

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.720
fan bases and teams like Vulcan who were
new to the scene and looking

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:31.580
make a name for themselves. And then
there was Dignitas, who were somewhere in

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:34.040
the middle
sometimes goofing around.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.400
sometimes wowing on stage.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:52.160
(Casting)

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:57.320
Dignitas were the LCS team that most
resembled a bunch of friends who were

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:01.200
just hanging out and playing League of
Legends at an extremely high level.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:05.160
(Casting)

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:09.720
(Casting)

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:15.930
(Casting)

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:19.050
(Casting)

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.820
(Casting)

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.360
Dignitas started their LCS run with a

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:31.320
whopping 16 and 5 record in their first
21 games of the spring split and qtpie

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:36.330
proved that he was a top-tier
North American AD carry. He was the

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:40.950
second in the league in KDA behind
Sneaky and his CS average was second

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:46.530
only to Doublelift. Dig stumbled at the
end of the season going 1-6 in their

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:51.880
final seven games to finish the season
with a 17-11 overall record.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.800
(Casting)

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:01.060
(Casting)

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:05.080
They were then immediately booted from the
playoffs by Good Game University.

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:11.520
(Casting)

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.980
(Casting)

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:19.440
The team's volatility continued into the summer split where they started

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:28.020
the Season 6-2 but finished 13-15, narrowly avoiding relegation. Heading into the 2014 season

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:32.600
KiWiKiD moved from top lane to support
and the team signed CruzerTheBruzer.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.880
This move marked an important moment in
Imaqtpie's career and was the peak

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:41.920
of qt's competitive prowess as a North
American AD carry

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:45.060
"I mean as bad as it is to say I'm never worried about any team,

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:50.200
like I know if I just like play my game I'm better than them."

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:56.640
(Casting)

00:08:56.679 --> 00:08:59.980
(Casting)

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:03.399
(Casting)

00:09:03.399 --> 00:09:06.519
(Casting)

00:09:06.519 --> 00:09:10.689
(Casting)

00:09:10.689 --> 00:09:13.800
(Casting)

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:16.700
(Casting)

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:21.120
At this time Dignitas was actually looking to
get rid of Kiwi from the roster entirely.

00:09:21.129 --> 00:09:25.360
"The original plan was to just remove him
from the team completely but I'd

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:31.269
actually asked our manager to keep Kiwi
on the team to make him my support like

00:09:31.269 --> 00:09:38.220
I took Kiwi from top lane barely playing
support into the support that he is now

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.360
and honestly I think he became a great
support."

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:43.060
2014 saw more of the same from

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:49.379
Dignitas. The team finished 12 and 16
during the season, placing fourth overall

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:54.699
The year was marred by roster shuffling
as both Shiphtur and Zionspartan

00:09:54.699 --> 00:09:59.649
joined the team while Scarra popped in
and out of the lineup. Dignitas would

00:09:59.649 --> 00:10:01.780
take 5th place in the playoffs.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:08.240
"We've always had problems with the team, that have stopped us from being as good as we could be.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:16.960
I honestly feel like, the people we have we could be the best. It's just our mentality is terrible."

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.360
It turns out when you're competing on a

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:23.939
national stage with four of your best
friends and everyone gets along

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:29.440
complacency can set in and it's that
complacency that imaqtpie it would

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.140
eventually capture as his on stream persona.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:46.580
That's right, qtpie was able to make not giving a crap a full time,

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:49.440
dedicated and lucrative business.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:07.560
But, professionally QT understood that the
LCS was going through a transition.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.880
"I wasn't meshing well with the scene, with where it was going.

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:15.480
Because, when I got into League it was completely different than how it is now."

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:19.320
More money was flowing into the league
and the pressure for teams to perform

00:11:19.329 --> 00:11:24.189
was greater than ever.
Organizations began to tinker with their

00:11:24.189 --> 00:11:28.629
rosters in search of more wins, breaking
up their stalwart players in favor of

00:11:28.629 --> 00:11:33.579
super teams. This is something qt
quickly realized he couldn't be a part

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:38.720
of. If he couldn't play with his friends
he couldn't play in the LCS.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:45.480
"I love this team, I f***ing couldn't stand it if we got anyone else or if I was on another team.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:51.520
Jesus Christ, f***cking people. Like, this team's great, I love 'em.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.160
That's why I want this to work."

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:56.160
In October 2014

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:00.440
imaqtpie announced that he would
not be re-signing with Dignitas.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:05.520
"So for me League has always been something that's just super fun.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:11.760
I am competitive by nature definitely, and I always strive to do my best to win.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:18.960
But I never had it in me to cut players for underperforming and things like that."

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:21.400
QT knew he still had the competitive

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:26.649
drive to play, so he took that drive and
put it towards his stream. Since making

00:12:26.649 --> 00:12:30.819
the jump from the LCS stage to his
living room chair QT has embraced

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:35.560
the lackadaisical attitude he
criticized Dignitas for and adopted it

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:40.200
into his personal streaming brand. He was
always known for his charismatic

00:12:40.209 --> 00:12:45.600
approach to the game even on-stage and
now he's turned that attitude into a day

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:51.760
job. Watching QT stream is an 8 hour long
amalgamation of professionalism.

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:03.340
and self-deprecating humor.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:20.800
He pulls your emotions in two

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:25.660
directions. First he reels you in with
his staggering streaming consistency,

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:31.180
huge viewership numbers and high
soloqueue skill level. Then he keeps you

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:35.980
coming back for his random tantrum like
outbursts and fun first approach to

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:37.420
playing League of Legends.

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:39.360
QT takes every classic nerd stereotype and
wields them as a means to his success.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:43.820
His ungroomed aesthetic and everyday
outfit of basketball shorts and a white

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:47.900
tee make him look more like the person
your parents warned you you'd become if

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:51.320
you didn't give up gaming than a
millionaire.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:15:01.220
What's most interesting is how self-aware he is about all of this. What best exemplifies this is his

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:04.780
ongoing virtual feud with Team Liquid's
Doublelift.

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:18.200
QT has routinely flamed NA's most famous pro AD carry, challenged him and claimed that he is

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:19.480
the superior player.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:26.000
"Do I have a retort? I have no idea what to say, I shit on Qtpie every time I see him in soloqueue.

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:56.720
This David versus Goliath style

00:15:56.720 --> 00:16:01.880
feud shows just how relevant QT is to
the League of Legends community. The joke

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:06.820
has reached as far as the LCS stage and
stoked the fires of Twitch chat

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.900
whenever Doublelift competes.

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:13.240
"I've heard some rumors going around that the real reason that you're back in the NA LCS

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:18.120
Is to avoid running into Qtpie in soloqueue. Can you provide with whether or not there's any truth to that."

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:24.420
"Dude, I was ranked higher than Qtpie for like five months, and the one time he's higher rank than me

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.740
he like has to rub it in my face.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:29.720
But, no. Qtpie is boosted garbage."

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:33.240
Even four years after his last LCS game, QT's

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:36.760
popularity still rivals some of the
game's best.

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:43.760
It's been almost four years since imaqtpie left Dignitas. In that time

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:47.920
he's accrued more viewership on Twitch
than any other League of Legends

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:53.930
streamer. He streams to almost 20,000
viewers each day around 50 hours a week

00:16:53.930 --> 00:17:00.110
and has more than 2 million followers. QT
did make a short return to the rift in

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:06.400
professional League of Legends with
Delta Fox in the summer of 2017. The team

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:10.960
was comprised of five notable streaming
personalities and competed in the NA

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:17.820
Challenger series as a subsidiary of LCS
team Echo Fox. Imaqtpie, Scarra,

00:17:17.839 --> 00:17:24.410
Dyrus, Voyboy and shiphtur made up a team
full of old guard LCS pros who were

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.100
apparently taking this project seriously.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:30.440
"Look you cannot argue that the talent of those players."

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:45.440
"Uh, in the past has been some of the best players in the game. Now coming back together to dust off their

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:48.000
their competitive skills."

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:07.880
"That was the first thing that came with ease for them of the competitive side was wanting to win."

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:24.360
"And the record may not show it, but I have to think that across the board it has reignited their competitive fires."

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:36.080
Unfortunately the meme stream

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.500
dream team as they called themselves

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:50.640
didn't secure a game win during the
entire split they competed in Challenger.

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:54.960
It definitely didn't help that they
fielded a team with three players who

00:18:54.960 --> 00:19:00.820
were primarily mid laners. All their
games were fairly similar each player

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:04.960
would often win their lane and then
Delta Fox would just get buried by their

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:10.240
opponents superior teamwork in a lot of
ways the Delta Fox experiment was

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:15.190
quintessential qtpie, they were a
team of solid players but they didn't

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:20.980
treat the team seriously enough to even
win a single game. Just as soon as it

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:26.290
started the Delta Fox experiment
finished in winless fashion. It was back

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:31.750
to the day-to-day streaming grind for QT
and his loyal subscribers. He's arguably

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:36.160
more famous than some of the best LCS
players in the world, commands more

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:41.380
attention and lives a more relaxed
lifestyle. QT's popularity shows the

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:46.600
breadth of the esports community and how
game adjacent personalities like him can

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:52.120
flourish with the right brand, tone and
work ethic which is the ever constant

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:57.190
paradigm with QT. He's a hard-working
self-made millionaire whose primary

00:19:57.190 --> 00:20:01.900
means of making money is acting like he
doesn't care about anything but having

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:04.000
fun all day long.

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:14.380
According to a March 2017 article
from Rolling Stone Imaqtpie

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:20.169
streaming career generates more than 2
million dollars per year in revenue. All

00:20:20.169 --> 00:20:25.720
that said the pro lifestyle has changed
a lot since QT's Dignitas days. We've

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:29.740
surpassed the era where a team could
attend a tournament and come home losing

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:36.130
money. In the new franchised iteration of
the NA LCS many pro players make a

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:40.929
livable wage and they're surrounded by
staff whose job it is to take care of

00:20:40.929 --> 00:20:45.909
them and their health. Imaqtpie
left the Wild West of the early days of

00:20:45.909 --> 00:20:50.740
League of Legends for the comfort of his
living room gaming setup and a whole lot

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:51.240
of money.

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:07.120
But since his departure the Wild
West has undergone a major facelift

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:13.559
which begs the question did Qtpie
leave some potential out on the rift?

00:21:13.559 --> 00:21:18.130
QT was even dethroned from his hard
lock at the top of League of Legends

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:22.720
independent streaming charts. Tyler1
has been unbanned from the game and has

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:28.630
made waves in his return to streaming. On
January 8th Tyler1 dismantled Faker's

00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:33.300
all-time individual League of Legends
streaming record with more than

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:37.020
380,000 concurrent
viewers

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:41.100
He finished the month with more
viewership than QT.

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:46.300
Maybe QT could have continued playing
pro and dominated LCS bot lanes like he

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:50.980
always wanted but his transition to
streaming has definitely worked out well

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:56.919
for him. The only thing we know for sure
is that whatever choice was wisest QT

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:59.520
doesn't care.

00:22:05.540 --> 00:22:07.040
"Bye!"

